---
import Legal from "../components/os/Legal.astro";
import { PORTFOLIO_DATA } from "../data/portfolio";
const { email } = PORTFOLIO_DATA.developer;
---

<Legal title="Privacy" description="What this site collects and what it doesn't." updated="6 November 2026">
  <p>This is a personal portfolio. It has no accounts, no ads and no analytics or tracking scripts.</p>

  <h2>What you send me</h2>
  <p>If you use the mail form, your name, email address and message are delivered to my inbox through <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree</a> when it is configured; otherwise the form opens your own mail app with the message pre-filled, and nothing is sent until you press send there. I use them only to reply to you, and I'll delete them if you ask.</p>

  <h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your light or dark theme choice (<code>goopros_mode</code>).</li>
    <li>A copy of my public GitHub data, cached for five minutes so the page loads faster.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Nothing here leaves your device, and clearing site data removes it.</p>

  <h2>Other services the page talks to</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Vercel hosts the site and keeps standard server logs.</li>
    <li>Your browser fetches my public repos from the GitHub API and my contribution graph from github-contributions-api.jogruber.de.</li>
    <li>Fonts load from Google Fonts.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Each of these sees your IP address as part of a normal web request and has its own privacy policy.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
